t (Slice 5), the nodule appears to be about a small fraction of the image width. I can approximate with proportions. It looks about 1/15th to 1/20th of the image width. If I split the image width into eighths, it looks to be about half an eighth. That's about 4 mm. Let me re-measure carefully. Yes, roughly 4 mm is my best estimate.\n\nSo, I'm thinking this is a **Nodule**. It looks like a discrete roughly spherical opacity that emerges and disappears over a few slices without continuing as a tubular structure. The approximate diameter is **4 mm**."
